[Music]  is briefing his soldiers on their  mission  they will escort civilians to banibango  a town near the jazz border with mali  a delicate mission armed groups have  attacked the town many times in the last  few years  at the command center lieutenant colonel  sami nomani and his team analyze the  latest intelligence from the region  samino shows me the 330 kilometer long  border area where the islamic state in  the greater sahara is active the  icy-linked armed group is seen as the  biggest security threat in the region  its leader abul walida saharawi was  killed in a drone strike in august last  year  general muhammad tumba and the 2000  soldiers under his command have been in  the battlefield for years but the fight  is far from over  difficulty  the biggest challenge we're facing is  that there is no malian or burkinabe  army on the other side of the border so  we can talk and plan attacks for the  last five years the malian army  retreated from the area and we're acting  on our own  outgunned the army relies heavily on  intelligence from foreign troops  this has become a forward base for  nigeria's army fighting against iceland  al-qaeda affiliates in the sahaja region  they're backed by american and european  special forces but a few kilometers  north towards the border with mali  armed groups are expanding they continue  to control a vast  territory now they are threatening to  take the fight south towards guinea  ivory coast and senegal  for years niger mali and pokina faso  have been trying to stop a rise in  attacks by armed groups  here in this camp the displaced have  been waiting for security to improve in  the border area but many traumatized by  the conflict  are afraid to return  i was looking after my sheep when  fighters on motorbikes stopped me they  saw a pen in my pocket and thought i was  an informant they blindfolded me and  beat me i lost my sheep and ever since  i've been here in this camp  for the time being the army remains on  alert after suffering major setbacks in  the last few years armed groups are now  forging new alliances finding new  recruits and hoping to establish a state  of their own across west africa and the  sahel  al-jazeera the town of wallam in  southwest niger

